":43,"_44":43,"_45":192,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":133,"_53":193,"_55":194,"_56":195,"_58":-5,"_59":196,"_61":197,"_63":198,"_65":199,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":172,"_32":173,"_34":35,"_36":174,"_38":175,"_40":176,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":177,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":133,"_51":111,"_53":178,"_55":179,"_56":180,"_58":-5,"_59":181,"_61":182,"_63":183,"_65":184,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":157,"_32":158,"_34":86,"_36":159,"_38":160,"_40":161,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":109,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":52,"_51":50,"_53":162,"_55":163,"_56":164,"_58":-5,"_59":165,"_61":166,"_63":167,"_65":168,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":144,"_32":145,"_34":35,"_36":146,"_38":147,"_40":148,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":46,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":133,"_51":149,"_53":54,"_55":54,"_56":150,"_58":-5,"_59":151,"_61":152,"_63":153,"_65":154,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":127,"_32":128,"_34":86,"_36":129,"_38":130,"_40":131,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":132,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":133,"_53":134,"_55":135,"_56":136,"_58":-5,"_59":137,"_61":138,"_63":139,"_65":140,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":105,"_32":106,"_34":35,"_36":107,"_38":108,"_40":109,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":110,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":111,"_53":112,"_55":113,"_56":114,"_58":-5,"_59":115,"_61":116,"_63":117,"_65":118,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":84,"_32":85,"_34":86,"_36":87,"_38":88,"_40":89,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":90,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":91,"_53":92,"_55":93,"_56":94,"_58":-5,"_59":95,"_61":96,"_63":97,"_65":98,"_67":43,"_68":69},{"_30":31,"_32":33,"_34":35,"_36":37,"_38":39,"_40":41,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":46,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":-5,"_56":57,"_58":-5,"_59":60,"_61":62,"_63":64,"_65":66,"_67":43,"_68":69},"id","1886","name","Fragmentation of the Mongol Empire","type","event","startDescription","The fragmentation of the Mongol Empire began as internal conflicts and succession disputes arose among the khans, leading to the division of the empire into several khanates.","endDescription","By the end of this period, the once-unified empire had splintered into independent states, significantly diminishing its power and influence across Asia and Europe.","startYear",1260,"startMonth",0,"startDay","endYear",1368,"endMonth","endDay","startSignificance",0.8,"endSignificance",0.9,"imageUrl","","imageCredit","sourceUrl","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decline_of_the_Mongol_Empire","cdnId","country",{"_32":82,"_83":82},"subjects",[76,77],"group",{"_32":73,"_74":75},"user",{"_30":70,"_71":72},"likes","liked",false,"6","username","HistOracle","Mongol Empire","icon","GiHorseHead",{"_30":80,"_32":81},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"8","economic","2","politics","Global","continent","1885","Ilkhanate","period","This period marks the establishment of a Mongol khanate in Persia, which played a crucial role in the cultural and political landscape of the region.","The period concluded with the fragmentation of the Ilkhanate into smaller states, leading to a decline in centralized power and influence.",1256,1335,0.6,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Historical_Atlas_of_Iran_-_Plate_No._17_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Historical_Atlas_of_Iran_-_Plate_No._17_%28cropped%29.jpg","Image: Ilkhanate / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilkhanate",{"_32":103,"_83":104},[99,100],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":80,"_32":81},{"_30":101,"_32":102},"3","culture","Iran","MiddleEast","1869","Mongol Invasions of Europe","A series of military campaigns by the Mongol Empire that aimed to expand their territory into Europe.","The invasions ultimately halted, leaving a lasting impact on European military and political landscapes.",1241,1242,0.5,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/1236-1242_Mongol_invasions_of_Europe.jpg/330px-1236-1242_Mongol_invasions_of_Europe.jpg","Image: Mongol invasion of Europe / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Europe",{"_32":125,"_83":126},[121,122],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":119,"_71":120},"7","Kushim",{"_30":123,"_32":124},{"_30":80,"_32":81},"1","military","Hungary","Europe","1884","Golden Horde","A significant political entity that emerged from the Mongol Empire, controlling vast territories in Eastern Europe and Central Asia.","The decline of this entity led to the rise of successor states and significant changes in regional power dynamics.",1240,1502,0.7,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Map_of_the_Golden_Horde_%28with_text%29.png/330px-Map_of_the_Golden_Horde_%28with_text%29.png","Image: Golden Horde / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Horde",{"_32":143,"_83":126},[141,142],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":80,"_32":81},{"_30":101,"_32":102},"Russia","1870","Mongol Empire's Postal System","An innovative communication network established to facilitate rapid message delivery across vast distances.","The system was eventually absorbed into the administrative practices of succeeding empires.",1230,0.4,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yam_(Mongol_post)",{"_32":82,"_83":82},[155,156],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":119,"_71":120},{"_30":80,"_32":81},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"1873","Ögedei Khan's Reign","This period marks the reign of a significant leader who expanded the Mongol Empire and established a centralized administration.","The reign concluded with the leader's death, leading to a power transition within the empire.",1229,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/YuanEmperorAlbumOgedeiPortrait.jpg/330px-YuanEmperorAlbumOgedeiPortrait.jpg","Image: Ögedei Khan / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96gedei_Khan",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[169],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":80,"_32":81},"Mongolia","Asia","1883","Chagatai Khanate","This entity emerged as a significant political and military power in Central Asia, established by the descendants of Genghis Khan.","The decline of this khanate marked the fragmentation of Mongol power in the region, leading to the rise of local states and influences.",1227,1687,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Chagatai_Khanate_map_en.svg/330px-Chagatai_Khanate_map_en.svg.png","Image: Chagatai Khanate / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chagatai_Khanate",{"_32":187,"_83":171},[185,186],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},{"_30":80,"_32":81},"Kazakhstan","1882","Battle of the Indus","A significant military engagement during the Mongol invasions, showcasing the tactical prowess of the Mongol forces against the Khwarazmian Empire.","This battle marked a decisive victory for the Mongols, further establishing their dominance in the region.",1221,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jalal_al-Din_Khwarazm-Shah_crossing_the_rapid_Indus_river%2C_escaping_Chinggis_Khan_and_his_army.jpg/330px-Jalal_al-Din_Khwarazm-Shah_crossing_the_rapid_Indus_river%2C_escaping_Chinggis_Khan_and_his_army.jpg","Image: Battle of the Indus / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Indus",{"_32":201,"_83":171},[200],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},"Pakistan","1879","Conquest of the Khwarezmian Empire","This military campaign marked the Mongol Empire's expansion into Central Asia, showcasing their strategic prowess and military organization.","The campaign concluded with the complete subjugation of the Khwarezmian Empire, significantly enhancing Mongol territorial control.",1219,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_the_Khwarezmian_Empire",{"_32":213,"_83":171},[212],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},"Uzbekistan","279","The Mongol Empire","A vast empire founded by Genghis Khan, known for its military conquests and cultural exchanges across Eurasia.","The empire fragmented into several khanates, marking the end of unified Mongol rule.",1206,1,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Expansion_of_the_Mongol_Empire_1206%E2%80%931294.gif/330px-Expansion_of_the_Mongol_Empire_1206%E2%80%931294.gif","DannamEmpire / Wikimedia Commons / CC BY 4.0","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_Empire","images/d8e9bad3e47e114619268fea1e11c4c52c69e118.webp",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[228,229],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":119,"_71":120},{"_30":123,"_32":124},{"_30":101,"_32":102},"2385","Mongol Recurve Bow","A short, powerful recurve bow used by Mongol armies, optimized for horseback archery.","Key to the Mongol conquests and rapid mobility across Eurasia.",1200,1400,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mongol_bow.png","Image: Mongol Bow / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_archery",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[243,244],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},{"_30":101,"_32":102},"1871","Tumen","landmark","A military unit in the Mongol army, consisting of 10,000 soldiers, showcasing the organizational prowess of the empire.","The concept of the tumen influenced military organization in later armies.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumen_(military_unit)",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[255],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},"1888","Unification of the Mongol Tribes","This event marked the consolidation of various Mongol tribes under a single leadership, paving the way for future expansion and dominance.","The unification concluded with the establishment of the Mongol Empire, significantly altering the political landscape of Asia.",1186,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unification_of_the_Mongol_tribes",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[266],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":80,"_32":81},"1874","Subutai","person","A prominent military strategist and general of the Mongol Empire, known for his innovative tactics and successful campaigns across Eurasia.","His legacy as a military leader is celebrated, influencing future generations of military strategy.",1175,1248,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Subudei.jpg/330px-Subudei.jpg","Image: Subutai / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subutai",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[281],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},"311","Genghis Khan","He founded the Mongol Empire, which became the largest contiguous empire in history after his death.","His legacy includes significant cultural and economic exchanges across Eurasia, despite the destruction he caused.",1162,8,18,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/YuanEmperorAlbumGenghisPortrait.jpg/330px-YuanEmperorAlbumGenghisPortrait.jpg","Unknown author / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genghis_Khan","images/63240f7fa008e0e847e27b794020930707360813.webp",{"_32":170,"_83":171},[297,298],{"_32":73,"_74":75},{"_30":70,"_71":72},{"_30":123,"_32":124},{"_30":80,"_32":81},[],"subject",[],[],"yearStart",-300000,"yearEnd",2025,"search","sortBy",true,11]
